<title>ITALY: Finmeccanica sees debts rise by end-March.</title>
<headline>Finmeccanica sees debts rise by end-March.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian state-controlled defence and engineering group Finmeccanica said on Wednesday that its net debt rose to 6.588 trillion lire at end-March compared to 5.113 trillion at end-1996 and 6.838 trillion at end-1995.</p>
<p>The group's chairman Fabiano Fabiani told the group's shareholders' meeting that the cause of the increased debt was the acquisition of railway equipment company Breda Ferroviaria for around 600 billion lire.</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129502</p>
